    {
      "name": "brian-armstrong/fec",
      "type": "repo",
      "brief": "A Rust library for forward error correction, on the list with GitHub and HackerNews agreeing. Error-correction code is infrastructure nobody adopts casually \u2014 it either solves a problem someone has or it sits unused \u2014 so the thing to watch is not stars but whether anyone depends on it. No package downloads yet, which is the number that would turn this from interesting to real.",
